# K4510: a dead-key console layout so the stick can type accents, the same as
# the desktop build gets from the host layout (Doc, 2026-09-10).  SDL's own
# console keyboard (KMSDRM/evdev) composes from the kernel keymap that
# console-setup builds from this file, then hands the machine the accented
# character as text -- the very SDL_TEXTINPUT path the desktop uses.
#
# US-International with dead keys:  ' e -> é   ` a -> à   ^ e -> ê
#                                   " u -> ü   ~ n -> ñ   (a space after a
#                                   dead key gives the plain ' ` ^ " ~).
# Canadian French instead:  set XKBLAYOUT="ca"  and clear XKBVARIANT.
XKBMODEL="pc105"
XKBLAYOUT="us"
XKBVARIANT="intl"
XKBOPTIONS=""
BACKSPACE="guess"
